label chapter_two:

    scene bg classroom
    with fade

    narrator "Week four."
    narrator "You've started arriving seven minutes earlier than usual."
    narrator "You tell yourself it's to get a better seat."
    narrator "The seating hasn't changed in three years."

    narrator "Riya notices."

    show mcquiet at center_char

    riya "You're here early."

    mc "I'm always here early."

    riya "You're here {i}earlier.{/i}"

    narrator "You smile at her."
    narrator "The one that says 'you're overthinking it.'"
    narrator "She says nothing."
    narrator "People usually don't."

    narrator "Orion arrives four minutes after you."
    narrator "You don't look up."
    narrator "You know it's him because the chair sixty-three centimeters to your left move."

    orion "You're early."

    mc "I'm always early."

    orion "You're always earlier."

    narrator "You look up."

    mc "Are you and Riya coordinating?"

    orion "Who's Riya?"

    narrator "He's already opened his notebook."
    narrator "He genuinely doesn't know who Riya is."
    narrator "Riya has four seats behind him for three years."

    thought "He doesn't track people the way I do."
    thought "People are indentical to him."
    thought "Except he tracked that I was earlier than usual."
    thought "So that's not entirely true."
    thought "He's interesting."

    narrator "The teacher starts the lesson."
    narrator "And you start writing your notes like he does."

label chapter_two_test:

    scene bg classroom
    with dissolve

    narrator "Unit Test - Friday."
    narrator "You finishe twelve minutes early."
    narrator "You check your answers twice."
    narrator "Then you check a third time."
    narrator "Because you need to be sure."
    narrator "You always need to be sure."

    narrator "Orion sub,its at the same time as you."
    narrator "You both stand up simultaneously."
    narrator "The class notices."

    thought "Good, let them notice."
    thought "Wait.."
    thought "..why did I think that?"

    narrator "You walk out into the corridor."
    narrator "He falls into the step beside you."
    narrator "Neither of you planned this."

    orion "How did you find question five?"

    mc "Fine.. dimensional analysis."

    orion "You wrote all the steps?"

    mc "Yes."

    orion "Good."

    narrator "You feel it land somewhere it shouldn't."

    thought "His approval affects my mood."
    thought "That's the problem."
    thought "That's a significant problem."
    thought "Log it and move on."

    mc "How did {i}you{/i} find it?"

    orion "Fine."

    mc "That's not an answer."

    orion "It's the same answer you gave me."

    narrator "You stop walking."
    narrator "He takes two more steps then stops too."
    narrator "Turn around."

    mc "I gave you a real answer."

    orion "You gave me a performance of a real answer."

    narrator "The corridor is very quiet."

    mc "What does that mean?"

    orion "It means 'fine' and 'straightforward' are words people use when they don't want they actually thought."

    narrator "You look at him."
    narrator "He looks back."
    narrator "Neither of you move."

    mc "And what did you actually think?"

    orion "That question five was testing whether you understood the concept or just memorized the method."
    orion "Most people memorized the method."

    mc "And you?"

    orion "I understood the concept."

    mc "And me?"

    narrator "A beat."

    orion "You understood the concept."
    orion "And then you wrote it like someone who memorized the method."
    orion "Because you knew that's what gets marked."

    narrator "Silence."

    narrator "He's right."

    mc "You pay a lot of attention to how I answer things."
